BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 358.3 Tm (Explanation: Impaired venous drainage raises capillary pressure and promotes movement of fluid from capillaries) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 345.2 Tm (into interstitial tissue.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.6 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 329.1 Tm (Other options: Higher plasma oncotic pressure or stronger lymphatic removal would oppose fluid accumulation.) Tj ET
BT /F1 7.2 Tf 0.43 0.45 0.49 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 314.5 Tm (Source: DOM-CVS-0027 | CIRCULATION 1, pp. 85-86, 90-93) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.7 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 291.3 Tm (19. A patient develops chronic swelling of an arm after axillary lymph nodes are removed. What is the main) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.7 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 277.6 Tm (reason?) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.3 Tf 0.1 0.33 0.58 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 260.9 Tm (Answer: D. Interstitial fluid and proteins cannot drain normally through lymph vessels.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 244.6 Tm (Explanation: Damage to lymphatic pathways reduces the return of interstitial fluid and proteins to the blood,) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 231.5 Tm (producing lymphoedema.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.6 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 215.4 Tm (Other options: Lymphoedema is caused by impaired lymph removal, not complete loss of arterial flow.) Tj ET
BT /F1 7.2 Tf 0.43 0.45 0.49 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 200.8 Tm (Source: DOM-CVS-0029 | CIRCULATION 1, pp. 60, 94-95; Regional, pp. 47-48) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.7 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 177.6 Tm (20. Why does walking help return blood from the leg veins to the heart?) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.3 Tf 0.1 0.33 0.58 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 160.9 Tm (Answer: A. Muscle contractions compress veins while valves limit backward flow.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 144.6 Tm (Explanation: Contraction of leg muscles compresses nearby veins. One-way venous valves direct the displaced blood) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 131.5 Tm (centrally, limiting pooling.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.6 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 115.4 Tm (Other options: Venous valves are passive one-way structures; muscle compression supplies the pumping action.) Tj ET
BT /F1 7.2 Tf 0.43 0.45 0.49 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 100.8 Tm (Source: DOM-CVS-0030 | CIRCULATION 1, pp. 97-98) Tj ET
